<$fill $name="body">

!! Pieces

|!Piece |!What it does |
|`dates.js`, `date-operators.js` |Date expressions (`today`, `+1d`, `mon`, …), formatting, day differences. Filter operators `wf-date` and `wf-days` |
|`check.js`, `action-wf-check.js` |Runs every area filter once (first match wins within a tab: one area per tab, several tabs possible), applies each tab's mutes, writes the snapshot. `<$action-wf-check/>`. Also the shared filter helpers: `runFilter` (a throw or a `Filter Error: …` result is an error, never an item) and `globalWidget`/`importWidget` (filters run under `\import [subfilter{$:/core/config/GlobalImportFilter}]`, like the page template) |
|`startup-check.tid` |Check on reload (`$:/tags/StartupAction/Browser`) |
|`actions.js` |Which tiles and groups the ring shows for one item (filters see the global and the engine functions); builds and runs an action (`wf.requires` checked first) |
|`ring-layer.js`, `ring-geometry.js` |The pointer gesture and the ring: plain DOM, laid out once per arc |
|`click-outside.js` |Startup module: a click outside dock and panel closes the panel |
|`engine.tid` |Shared `\function`s and `\procedure`s for dock, panel and item |
|`layer.tid`, `dock.tid`, `panel.tid`, `item.tid` |Page template layer, closed strip, open panel, one row |
|`edit-engine.tid` |Edit mode `\function`s and `\procedure`s: slugs, tag lists that skip the form buffer (`wf.tagged`, `wf.actions-all`, `wf.groups-all`, `wf.recipes-all`), area and tab operations, form open/save/duplicate/delete/close, `wf-escape` |
|`edit-panel.tid`, `area-card.tid` |Edit mode body of the panel: tabs, area cards with inline forms |
|`form.tid`, `action-form.tid`, `group-form.tid`, `info-picker.tid` |The floating form host (rendered by `layer.tid` while the form state exists), the two forms and the `wf.info` editor |
|`recipes/<name>/form.tid` |One form per shipped recipe |
|`live-filter.js`, `live-widget.js` |`<$wf-live>`: a filter evaluated once at render and, debounced 300 ms, when its text changes; never on other wiki changes |
|`datalist.js` |Startup module: adds `list=` to field-name inputs when they take the focus |
|`styles.tid`, `config/*`, `info/*`, `recipes/*`, `groups/*`, `actions/*` |Styles, defaults, shipped parts |

!! Data flow

# A check runs the area filters in tag order. Within a tab an item goes to the first area that matches; other tabs place it on their own. An item muted in a tab goes to that tab's muted list.
# The result is one JSON tiddler, the //snapshot// (`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/snapshot`). Dock and panel only read it.
# A drag asks `actions.select` for the ring: every action whose filter returns something for this item, grouped by `wf.group`.
# A release runs the action string with the item's variables, then writes an //acted mark// and checks again.

!! State tiddlers

|!Tiddler |!Content |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/snapshot` |`{"checked", "areas": {area: [items]}, "muted": {tab: [items]}, "errors": {area: message}}`; the unnamed tab's key is `$:/rimir/work-focus/no-tab` |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/acted` |`{area: {item: mark}}` – per area, so an item acted on in one tab is a plain row in another; cleared by a reload or ↻, an item's marks by unmuting it |
|`$:/rimir/work-focus/mutes` |`{tab: {item: "YYYYMMDD"}}` (General = `$:/rimir/work-focus/no-tab`), saved with the wiki (not under `$:/state/`, which TW does not sync): the day the item shows again in that tab. An older entry `{item: "YYYYMMDD"}` (from 0.1.1) mutes in every tab until it expires; unmuting it removes it |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/open` |`yes` while the panel is open |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/more/<area>` |`yes` after "+ N more" was clicked |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/show-muted` |`yes` while the muted list is shown |
|`$:/state/rimir/work-focus/tab` |The active tab (per session; not saved) |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/edit` |`yes` while the panel is in edit mode |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/edit-view` |`areas` (default) or `actions` |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/edit-area` |The area whose card is open |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/form` |Form state: `kind` (`action` or `group`), `target` (blank = new), `item`, `area`, `side` (`left` or `right`), `value` (the tile clicked in the ring, highlighted in the tiles editor), `left`/`top` (px, set by the ring: the form sits next to it; blank = at the window edge of `side`) |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/form/buffer` |The copy the form edits. The transient field `wf-form.default` is applied and removed on Save |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/form/tiles`, `…/form/tile-label` |Tiles editor inputs (add row; the label being edited with its old value) |
|`$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/confirm` |The second click of a delete |

!! Edit mode

* ''Areas'' edit the area tiddler in place. The card's count is the raw filter count from `<$wf-live>`: no first-match placement, drafts counted, so it can be higher than the dock chip.
* ''Actions and groups'' edit a copy. `wf-form-open` reads the variables `kind`, `target`, `item`, `area`, `preset` (a JSON string of fields for a new one) and `side`, writes the form state and fills the buffer. Save writes the tiddler (`$action-createtiddler … $overwrite`) and closes the form; closing otherwise writes nothing.
* ''Delete'' on a shipped action or group sets `wf.hidden: yes` (hidden, not gone); "↺ Shipped" in the form removes the override and restores the shipped one. A new one is deleted for real.
* ''Switching the recipe'' keeps the old recipe's `wf.*` fields in the tiddler.
* ''Default of group'' (action form) can only set a default; clear it in the group form.
* ''Replaces'' edits one title, although `wf.replaces` may be a list.
* ''Recipe forms'': `<recipe title>/form` is rendered with `currentTiddler` = the buffer and the variables `item`, `area`, `date-field`. A bridge plugin adds a form for its own recipe by shipping that tiddler.
* ''Ring in edit mode'': pinned after release, ✎ badges, "+ group" and "+ add…", hidden actions dimmed. While a form is open hovering does not fan or close arcs (a click does). The ring rebuilds after a save. The 6 group cap with "⋯ More" applies in edit mode too.

!! Limits built in

At most 6 groups on the first ring (the rest under "⋯ More") and 3 levels of nesting.

